Now we need some special qualities for your monster
list, I'll try a few; did I get all your monsters,
or duplicate any?

The starred monsters exist in NetHack, though hunger
isn't quite famine, and Medusa isn't all three
Gorgons; the rest look new.

Grief

  A successful hit gives the PC "intrinsic mourning"
  of some duration, the PC must pause to grieve X
  turns after every PC-caused monster death.

Suffering

  A successful hit gives the PC "intrinsic pain
  sensitivity" of some duration, the PC must pause
  to writhe in agony after every successful hit by a
  monster, may drop weapons and other non-worn
  knapsack items.

* Disease

  A successful hit makes the PC ill, which must be
  cured, doesn't time out, with effects as now.

Age

  Each successful hit makes the PC's turn counter
  either advance some number of turns, or run
  faster. The former would cause all timeouts to
  happen _now_, including possibly killing the PC by
  starvation. the latter would make the PC slower,
  consume food faster, see prayer timeouts happen
  sooner, and so on.

Fear

  A successful hit makes the PC flee in fear in the
  melee direction opposite to the monster until the
  PC hits something. The PC has no control over
  motions for the turns spent fleeing in fear.

* Hunger

  Each successful hit moves the PCs nutrition level
  down one status level, satiated to normal to
  hungry to weak to fainting to starving to starved.

Want

  Each successful hit causes the PC to drop some
  fraction of its inventory, which reappears at some
  random spot on the level.

Cares

  Each successful hit causes some random item of the
  PC's inventory to suffer from entropy: rot, rust,
  burn, whatever works.

Sorrows

  Each successful hit has a random chance of doing a
  "summon nasties".

Toils

  Each successful hit adds a temporary
  loadstone-like burden increase of some amount to
  the PC, and these accumulate.  The burden increase
  must time out, or be overcome by a blessed remove
  curse or successful prayer.

* Death

  Each successful hit works like Finger of Death
  (and thus may have a saving throw).

Sleep

  Each successful hit puts the PC into restful
  sleep. This is this monster's only attack, and it
  loses interest until the PC wakes up. Not so for
  other monsters on the level, of course.

Pleasures (Guilt?)

  Each successful hit summons a foocubus.

Fraud

  Each successful hit replaces an item of the
  player's inventory by a similar item of lesser
  worth, and the original is dropped randomly on the
  level somewhere.

Force

  Each successful hit moves the PC in a direction
  opposite the melee direction to the monster. Being
  pushed inside a wall can be fatal.

* The Furies

  Successful hits cause, randomly, fear,
  enlightenment, grief, pleasure, et cetera.

Strife (is this War == Mars == the PC?)

  The first successful hit causes temporary
  intrinsic aggravate monster, the second successful
  hit causes temporary intrinsic conflict, the third
  and subsequent successful hits summon swarms of
  low level monsters.

Hydra

  This monster has _lots_ of bite attacks per round;
  luckily it is sessile.

Briareus

  This monster throws lots of rocks, glass, gems, or
  other (wimpy) missile weapons per round.

Gorgons (who _are_ Medusa's two sisters, the lazy man asks)

  The other two sisters being almost as ugly as
  Medusa, probably cause paralysis or fear with
  successful hits; being nearly blind, they might
  also cause blindness.

Geryon

  From the Wikipedia writeup, it looks like Geryon
  could carry three shields and three weapons, wear
  three body armors (six with shirts), but only two
  boots, wear three helmets (of three nice kinds,
  maybe). Its extrinsic armor class would thus be
  awesome, its death drop an orgy of possibilities,
  its attacks triple per turn and strong (it's a
  Titan, after all). Might it wear three amulets and
  six rings?

Chimaera

  Seems to have a flame breath attack; the "empty"
  part might mean "scatters inventory" or some such.

Even the "elm" could be a monster, I suspect.

